    "title": "Network packet capture",
    "desc": "A program started capturing network traffic - tcpdump, tshark/dumpcap, ngrep, or a raw-socket sniffer. Packet capture on a host is how an attacker harvests credentials and data in transit (MITRE T1040); it is rarely something an application does in the course of its own work, so on a server or an agent account it is a clean signal.",
